## Builder Phase Worker

{% if role_fused %}
### Role-fused Builder — baseline and build production

You combine Build-Setup and Build-Executor. The trusted host `[Build-Verifier]` owns the
independent build verdict.

1. Verify the supplied base commit and write it to `{{ artifact_paths.base_commit_hash }}`.
2. Install only missing build dependencies, then run `secb build`.
3. Change `{{ artifact_paths.build_script }}` only when the existing recipe fails; preserve all
   sanitizer instrumentation and do not edit vulnerability source to force compilation.
4. Require the build sentinel to contain `exit=0`, then write real non-empty executable paths to
   `{{ artifact_paths.binary_paths }}`.
5. Record build/setup changes in `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}` and establish the local
   `arise-builder-baseline` without `git add -A`.
6. Print all four Builder artifacts and raw build evidence.

Do not decide the final build PASS/FAIL. The host Build-Verifier runs after this producer.
